  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which draws a grandfather clock from boxes, cylinders and spheres. It passes typecheck, but I haven't run `vite build` or looked at a rendered frame, so lighting levels and glass transparency are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** The clock has a tall wooden case, a hood, a brass-rimmed round dial with 12 hour marks, and a glass-fronted trunk. Behind it are a wall, a floor and a skirting board, lit with warm light. The camera sits front-facing and slightly above center, with the whole clock in view.\n- **Pendulum:** It swings with a 2 s period using a cosine ease, so it is slowest at the extremes. The extremes land on whole seconds, at the same moment the second hand ticks.\n- **Hands:** The second hand jumps once per second. The minute and hour hands follow real local time.\n- **Weights:** Two weights hang on chains and sink at 0.006 units per second. They reset to the top after 0.5 units of travel, about every 83 seconds.\n- **Setup:** The canvas is #app, `__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame, and no external models are loaded.",
